  "custom_logic_notes": "The EA uses WPR[1] (previous completed bar) for signal generation, not WPR[0]. The position gate checks both no existing buy position (for longs) and no existing sell position (for shorts) separately via PositionType enumeration. The digit adjustment multiplier (DigK) scales SL/TP by 10 for 5-digit brokers (common for JPY pairs and modern 5-digit forex pricing). WPR levels are symmetric around the midpoint: the overbought threshold is -InpWPRLevel and the oversold threshold is -100+InpWPRLevel, meaning with default InpWPRLevel=70, sell when WPR is below -70 (overbought) and buy when WPR is above -30 (oversold).",
